---
import CopyButton from "./CopyButton.astro";
import { CLIENTS } from "./clients";

const command = "kivgraph mcp install --scope user";
---

<div class="grid grid-cols-1 items-baseline gap-10 lg:grid-cols-2">
  <div>
    <p class="max-w-[68ch] text-sm leading-6 text-gray-300">
      One MCP server over stdio, and the same structural context in every client
      that speaks the protocol. <code>kivgraph mcp install</code> detects the
      agents on the machine, lets you pick, and writes the entry — with a
      backup beside the file it edits and <code>--dry-run</code> to see the
      change first.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-10 border border-rule bg-panel">
      <div
        class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4 border-b border-rule px-4 py-2 text-xs text-gray-400"
      >
        <span>register the client</span>
        <CopyButton value={command} event="client_connect_copy" />
      </div>
      <pre
        class="px-4 py-3 text-xs leading-5 whitespace-pre-wrap break-all"><code><span class="text-graph-exact select-none">$ </span>{command}</code></pre>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-3 max-w-[68ch] text-xs leading-5 text-gray-400">
      The scope is <code>user</code> or <code>project</code>. Nothing is
      installed inside a repository you registered, and the command neither
      initialises Kivgraph nor indexes anything.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div>
    <ul class="border-t border-rule font-mono">
      {
        CLIENTS.map((client) => (
          <li class="grid grid-cols-1 items-baseline gap-x-6 gap-y-1 border-b border-rule py-3 text-xs sm:grid-cols-[10rem_minmax(0,1fr)]">
            <a
              href={client.page}
              class="text-gray-100 underline decoration-rule underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-accent-200"
            >
              {client.label}
            </a>
            <div>
              <p class="text-gray-400">
                <code>--target {client.target}</code>
              </p>
              {client.note !== undefined && (
                <p class="mt-1 text-gray-400">{client.note}</p>
              )}
            </div>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-5 max-w-[68ch] text-xs leading-5 text-gray-400">
      Twelve tools are registered once a generation is published. Before that
      the server registers only <code>index_project</code> and says so, rather
      than offering eleven tools that would have nothing to answer from.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-5 text-xs">
      <a
        href="/mcp/clients/"
        class="text-accent-200 underline underline-offset-4"
        >every client, with its configuration path</a
      >
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
